0..76 Comment "// What `univalence`\'s two owed laws state, read through transport, holds by"
77..154 Comment "// conversion: `ua` after `idtoequiv` transports forward and back as the path"
155..230 Comment "// does, at every path between types, and `idtoequiv` after `ua` transports"
231..304 Comment "// forward as the record\'s map, at every record. The laws themselves stay"
305..382 Comment "// owed: two paths between types that transport alike are not one path, and a"
383..450 Comment "// record\'s inverses are not determined by its map without function"
451..484 Comment "// extensionality from a homotopy"
485..542 Comment "// (`pathological/identity/univalence-owed.gandr`, #520)."
544..618 Comment "// Univalence over the user universe: `fwdAlong`, `bwdAlong`, `idtoequiv`."
